  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two scopes",
      "items": [
        "The wrapper resolves the Operation Context once per request, shared with the rate limit, and begins the request scope's Operation with no Module.",
        "The Gateway checks that its Module owns the command, then begins a second scope's Operation with that Module, which routes it to the Module's Unit of Work.",
        "In the monolith template the endpoint takes IDispatcher from the request scope: one scope, no Gateway."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The dispatcher's order",
      "items": [
        "It binds the Host's clock and opens the log scope, then runs every authorizer and the validator; a failure returns Errors before any Unit of Work. Once they pass, the Operation is authorized, and continuing its context is a trusted continuation.",
        "For the outermost command it starts the Unit of Work; the request id's key is reserved inside it, so a repeat waits, then replays the first success.",
        "A request id on a command without [Idempotent] throws. After RunAsync returns, a success on a rollback-only Operation throws too."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "One problem response (ADR 0008)",
      "items": [
        "ToHttpResult maps a failed Result to RFC 9457 with every Error: validation 400, forbidden 403, not found 404, conflict 409, anything else 500.",
        "An exception becomes a 500 problem response; a refused Idempotency-Key, a 400 whose detail states the rule.",
        "An empty-bodied refusal of the pipeline, 401, 403 or 429, is written as the same problem response."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "A cached query",
      "items": [
        "Only the Operation's outermost query, while it is not rollback-only, reads and stores entries, keyed by its Actor, tenant and UI culture.",
        "A command's declared tags are evicted only after its Operation commits; a rollback evicts nothing."
      ]
    }
  ]
